{
  "dom_id": "question-133832",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14168483/assets/bef0863eeb7006d89cc92a80be2a84e6ea09bca14cbb29c15af4f2e01e79045f.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            Jacob's neighbor to the south, Tom, has a land plot of area ${x}^{2}+x-2$ square meters, as shown in the picture. Given that the length of Tom's plot of land is $x-1$ meters, what is the width of the plot in terms of $x?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Tom's plot width is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nmeters.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the required width, we need to factor the expression ${x}^{2}+x-2.$\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of the constant term $(-2).$ The constant term is negative, so that means one of the factors is negative, and the other is positive:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & \\times (-2) \\\\ (-1) & \\times 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find which factor pair adds up to the coefficient of the linear term $1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+(-2) & =-1 & \\times  \\\\ -1+2 & =1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the factor pair identified above, write the linear term as $x=2x-x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-2 & ={x}^{2}+2x-x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the first two terms and the last two terms separately, and then factor the expression completely:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x-x-2 & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x)+(-x-2) & = \\\\ x(x+2)-(x+2) & = \\\\ (x-1)(x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the width must be $x+2$ meters. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14168483/assets/d2b543dc559c23c191231543701ffb05a7c8350bc066a047b836fe64766c7289.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
